{"name":"Abidjan","slug":"abidjan","region":"Africa","lat":5.36,"lon":-4.01,"seasons":{"DJF":{"season_name":"Dec 2026–Feb 2027","years":[1951,1952,1953,1954,1955,1956,1957,1958,1959,1960,1961,1962,1963,1964,1965,1966,1967,1968,1969,1970,1971,1972,1973,1974,1975,1976,1977,1978,1979,1980,1981,1982,1983,1984,1985,1986,1987,1988,1989,1990,1991,1992,1993,1994,1995,1996,1997,1998,1999,2000,2001,2002,2003,2004,2005,2006,2007,2008,2009,2010,2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023,2024,2025],"roni_lead":[-0.38,0.98,0.04,0.84,-0.31,-1.31,-0.14,1.16,0.24,0.04,0.08,-0.16,-0.3,1.06,-0.64,1.86,-0.03,-0.08,0.56,0.67,-0.57,-0.4,1.82,-1.63,-0.45,-0.95,1.04,0.89,-0.08,0.52,-0.06,-0.17,2.03,-0.9,-0.61,-0.18,1.0,1.2,-1.71,-0.23,0.27,1.2,0.1,0.46,0.97,-0.93,-0.25,2.22,-1.33,-1.06,-0.55,-0.18,1.18,0.17,0.7,-0.18,0.73,-1.33,-0.38,0.86,-1.61,-0.91,0.21,-0.22,0.35,2.03,-0.96,-0.82,0.62,0.15,-1.37,-1.08,-1.1,1.3,-0.76],"paragraph":"Dec–Feb in Abidjan has warmed by about 0.25 °C per decade since 1951, roughly 1.9 °C in all, and the hottest days have warmed faster than the coldest (about 0.3 vs 0.2 °C per decade). There is a strong, well-established El Niño effect on temperature: after El Niño conditions in the preceding fall, Dec–Feb tends to run warmer, and El Niño accounts for about 35% of the year-to-year ups and downs. With this year's strong El Niño, that push is about 2 times a normal year-to-year swing, roughly as much warmth as 24 years of the long-term trend. Without El Niño, a Dec–Feb this warm would come about once every 54 years. El Niño moves the hottest days most: this season they are expected to shift by about 0.9 °C, against 0.4 °C for the coldest days. Dec–Feb rainfall has fallen by about 10% per decade. El Niño has a clear effect toward a drier season with fewer rainy days, and this year's shift is substantial. Relative humidity has fallen by about 0.4 points per decade, roughly 3 points since 1951; because warmer air holds more moisture, this does not necessarily mean the air is drier. El Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a less humid Dec–Feb, and this year's shift is substantial. For Dec 2026–Feb 2027, a warmer-than-normal season is very likely (more than 95% chance), about 1.2 °C above the 1991–2020 average; a drier-than-normal season is likely (about 85% chance), and a less humid season than normal is likely (about 85% chance). The El Niño expected for Sep–Nov 2026 is stronger than any in the record used here, so the outlook extends the historical relationship beyond what has been observed. This outlook is based on the El Niño strength expected for Sep–Nov 2026 and will be updated when it is observed in early December.","variables":{"temperature":{"normal_1991_2020":26.4837,"trend_per_decade":0.2471,"trend_p":0.0,"trend_total_since_1951":1.8532,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.2369,"enso_p":0.0,"confidence":"Strong","survives_fdr":true,"fraction_explained":0.3741,"intrinsic_sd":0.2872,"effect_this_season":0.5994,"effect_ratio":2.0869,"size":"Dominant","size_typical_el_nino":"Dominant","once_every_n_years_without_el_nino":54,"expected_anomaly_2027":1.1824,"forecast_mean":27.6661,"forecast_sd":0.3167,"p_below":0.0,"p_near":0.0008,"p_above":0.9992,"forecast_words":"Very likely (>95%): a warmer-than-normal season","within_record":false,"trend_part_2027":0.5829,"roni_upper_within_record":false,"years_of_warming_equivalent":24.2579,"percentiles":{"p05":{"trend_per_decade":0.1845,"trend_p":0.0,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.1456,"enso_p":0.0409,"confidence":"Clear","shift_this_season":0.3683,"lines_cross":false},"p50":{"trend_per_decade":0.2415,"trend_p":0.0,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.2229,"enso_p":0.0,"confidence":"Strong","shift_this_season":0.564,"lines_cross":false},"p95":{"trend_per_decade":0.3059,"trend_p":0.0,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.3636,"enso_p":0.0,"confidence":"Strong","shift_this_season":0.9199,"lines_cross":false},"tails":{"enso_difference":0.218,"enso_difference_p":0.0093,"trend_difference":0.1213,"t